  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a tank made of glass (refractive index <math><mn>1.5</mn></math> ) with a thick bottom. It is filled with a liquid of refractive index <math><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>.</mo></math> A student finds that, irrespective of what the incident angle <math><mi>i</mi></math> (see figure) is for a beam of light entering the liquid, the light reflected from the liquid glass interface is never completely polarized. For this to happen, the minimum value of <math><mi>&#956;</mi></math> is:<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/eifuxtqcpovatxmolgmigpjhuijueoiwbcibepjlijkpahegko.png\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Wopxa",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Cd7fB",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6gYCW",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3o78x",
      "text": "<math><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/wrdszehlkazjhgodgeswfkowszafgbaazattifyxzuxcoonyck.png\" /><br /><br />For reflected light not be completely polarized,<br /><br /><math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≠</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />For minimum <math><mi>μ</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>r</mi></math> is maximum. <math><mi>r</mi></math> is maximum when <math><mi>i</mi></math> is maximum i.e. <math><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>90</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><msup><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><msup><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.25</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>1.25</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.25</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2.25</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1.25</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
